In terms of behavioral characteristics, jaguars are solitary animals and are known to be highly territorial. They are ambush predators, using their camouflage to stalk prey from a distance before pouncing. Jaguars are also excellent swimmers and can dive underwater to hunt fish and other aquatic animals.

