Wild boars are characterized by their robust build, with a sturdy body and a muscular appearance. They have a broad head with a large snout, which is often used for rooting in the ground to search for food.

#### 2. Color Patterns and Markings:
Wild boars typically display a mottled coat with a mix of dark brown, black, and sometimes reddish-brown patches. Their coloration can vary depending on the subspecies and geographic location. Some individuals may also have lighter-colored underbellies or legs.

#### 3. Size and Proportions:
Wild boars are generally medium-sized animals, with males being larger than females. Males can weigh up to 200 kg, while females usually weigh around 100 kg. They have a stocky body with short legs and a relatively small head compared to their body size.

