Rock Beauties are often found in coral reefs, where they feed on algae and small invertebrates. They are known for their curious behavior, frequently approaching divers and swimmers. Their bright coloration serves as a warning to potential predators, as they are toxic due to their diet of algae and sponges. The Rock Beauty's unique identifying trait is its striking color pattern, which makes it easily distinguishable from other similar species.
